Workspace refactor in delivery order (@workspace-stages: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @workspace-development) { r_1YY2R9043QSH0PSNZ2K29SS2V9
Build the native Lince desktop one capability at a time. A Sand, an application surface, a room, a circuit board and a specimen can occupy the same workspace. Each keeps its identity as the user changes viewpoint, edits its source or chooses how much of it to load and simulate.

**Start here** [006 · Save a behavior choice on an occurrence](stages/006-save-a-behavior-choice-on-an-occurrence.lingua). This is the chosen delivery order. Each of the 190 numbered links below opens one stage with an observable result, implementation scope, completion checks and an evidence handoff. The first stage establishes a measurement reference. [110 · Core desktop acceptance](stages/110-use-the-refactored-desktop-as-one-workspace.lingua) proves that the earlier desktop capabilities work together. Optional recipes and separately selected research methods are labeled.

## Current position

Stage 001 passed on 2026-11-22. Its handoff includes the fixed-clock native replay, fresh-process reopen, three real-clock timing runs, five reviewed findings, ten fixture cases and the delivery contracts. Stage 002 also passed. The native desktop can save and reopen two placements of a shared part, with stable identities and recovery after an interrupted save. Stage 003 verified selection, movement, undo and reopening for an existing Room member linked to the scene. Stage 004 verified recovery of an accepted edit and rejection of a late measurement through the native Showoff and local Fiote tool. Stage 005 verified local definition import, shared dependencies and inspection of conflicting revisions with the source offline. Stage 006 is next. [Stage 005 proof](../../fixtures/workspace/stage05/README.md) · [Stage 004 proof](../../fixtures/workspace/stage04/README.md) · [Stage 003 proof](../../fixtures/workspace/stage03/README.md) [Stage 002 proof](../../fixtures/workspace/stage02/README.md) [November evidence](../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/resumption-2026-11-22/README.md) · [October audit](../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/completion-audit.json)

Legacy identifiers such as `01.W01`, `11a.T04` and `15a.T06` still identify original workflows and tasks. The 87 feature Records own the 276 task entries and their implementation boundaries. The 28 contract Records own fixtures, guarantees and composed acceptance. A task can span several numbered stages. Check it off in its owner Record only after every part has evidence. The card on which the last provider becomes available identifies the composed replay. [Technical dependencies](Workspace-Development.lingua#dependency-graph) · [Contract catalogue](Workspace-Contracts.lingua)

Every stage card inherits [Workspace refactor delivery](Workspace-Refactor.lingua), including the cumulative native showcase replay and the stage handoff.

## Picking up the next stage

1. Open the first unfinished stage in this order. Read its preceding handoff and the linked task and proof sections. Work on that one outcome. The feature graph still identifies technical prerequisites if the delivery order is ever revised. A character can already be built in a local room before any globe or photographic reconstruction.
2. Implement the ordinary native entry point and its actual data path. Use the card’s fixture and an independent expected result. Check applicable save/reopen, undo, permissions, failure recovery, resource limits and one earlier workflow affected by the change. New or changed edit panels follow the native left-edge, height and reachable-control requirements. [Desktop edit-panel rule](../Lince.lingua) · [Shared acceptance guidance](Workspace-Development.lingua#workflow-contracts-and-balanced-acceptance)
3. Record the revision, fixture, device/profile where relevant, runnable command, expected and observed results, limitations and a durable link to the evidence in the card. On a failed required check, record the failure, repair its earliest owner and replay affected work. Publish a package handoff when its owned stages and local proofs pass. Make representative timing measurements in an exclusive window after compilation. [Handoff and repair](Workspace-Development.lingua#dependency-driven-delivery-and-repair)
4. Follow the next link. An optional recipe or specialist method can be recorded as deferred when its scope has not been selected. A later stage that actually needs that provider waits for its verified handoff. Core desktop acceptance has its own explicit contributors. For a specialist package, recover the handoff for the selected law or coupling. For example, electrical heat feedback uses verified thermal coupling, and the acoustic study has independent evidence. Each deferred method needs its own reference, error and resource bounds before a claim of support.

## How detail works across the sequence

- A glowing object can keep an authored appearance. A functional lamp responds to a sensor event. A wired lamp responds to calculated electrical power. Place them together and inspect what drives each light. [045 · Functional lamp](stages/045-wire-a-functional-sensor-to-a-lamp.lingua) · [072 · Powered lamp](stages/072-light-a-lamp-from-a-simulated-power-source.lingua)
- A detailed board can expose a single sensor port while its internals are unloaded. The view, structural coverage, behavior model, numerical accuracy, clock and budget are separately inspectable choices. A validated transfer must preserve the declared outputs and state when changing models in flight. [046 · Per-occurrence policy](stages/046-choose-the-behavior-detail-of-one-occurrence.lingua) · [070 · Board as device](stages/070-use-a-whole-board-as-one-functional-device.lingua) · [074 · Live circuit transition](stages/074-change-circuit-fidelity-during-a-running-event.lingua) · [148 · Thermal transition](stages/148-switch-a-thermal-model-to-a-lumped-approximation.lingua)
- A user can inhabit a local character, enter a component’s view, possess an object temporarily, or refine a region of a coarse world. The source stays editable at its own scale. The same place data can be placed in a fictional world. [035 · Character control](stages/035-navigate-as-a-supplied-character.lingua) · [044 · Cross-scale exploration](stages/044-enter-an-objects-available-scale-and-return.lingua) · [048 · Temporary play](stages/048-play-as-an-object-in-a-temporary-trial.lingua) · [083 · Portable place fragment](stages/083-move-a-fragment-into-a-different-world.lingua)

